1
00:00:09,965 --> 00:00:16,075
A job is rarely one thing, and the person
who raised it usually knows more than the

2
00:00:16,075 --> 00:00:16,885
title says.

3
00:00:17,337 --> 00:00:22,956
A checklist is how you say what finished
means, before somebody drives out there.

4
00:00:23,407 --> 00:00:27,587
Item by item, in the order
somebody would actually do them.

5
00:00:29,505 --> 00:00:33,360
They get ticked on site, from
the phone, as the work is done.

6
00:00:33,812 --> 00:00:40,360
When one job needs two visits, or two
trades, it splits rather than sprawls.

7
00:00:40,811 --> 00:00:46,244
Each part is a job in its own right,
with its own person and its own finish.

8
00:00:46,695 --> 00:00:53,656
And this is where what comes back from
site lands — the photographs, the paperwork,

9
00:00:53,656 --> 00:00:55,333
whatever was signed.

10
00:00:55,786 --> 00:01:00,848
All of it on one page, months later,
without anybody having kept a folder.

